        cross-platform attribution tooling. <strong>You use these tools on
        your own marketing accounts, your own stores, and your own
        data</strong>. The Service does not run your business for you, and
        you remain the decision-maker on all spend, creative, pricing, and
        customer-facing actions.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Not a licensed adviser</h2>
      <p>
        {legalEntity.name} does not provide legal, tax, accounting, or
        regulated marketing advice. Any benchmarks, recommendations, or
        playbooks produced by the Service are informational. If you need
        advice tailored to your situation, consult a licensed professional.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old and authorised to act on behalf
        of any business, store, or ad account you connect to the Service.
        The Service is not offered to persons located in countries subject
        to comprehensive sanctions administered by OFAC, the Government of
        Canada under the Special Economic Measures Act, the UN Security
        Council, the European Union, or HM Treasury.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your accounts &amp; connected platforms</h2>
      <p>
        Where you connect Meta, Amazon, Shopify, or any other third-party
        platform, you authorize the Service to read and (where you grant
        the scope) write to those accounts on your behalf. You remain bound
        by each platform's terms of service and content policies —
        violations are your responsibility, not ours. We will not knowingly
        use the Service to help you breach a platform's rules, commit ad
        fraud, or deceive consumers.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Past performance &amp; case studies</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Historical performance of client engagements is not a
        guarantee of future results for your account.</strong> Metrics in
        case studies are attributed to the source of truth (Meta Ads
        Manager, Shopify, Amazon Seller Central) and rounded to two
        significant figures. Client names appear only with written
        consent; otherwise they are anonymized.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Fees &amp; subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Fees and plan inclusions are disclosed at the point of purchase.
        Fees are <strong>non-refundable except where required by
        applicable law</strong>, including Ontario's Consumer Protection
        Act, 2002. You may cancel at any time; cancellation stops future
        billing.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Licence &amp; intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        "Glitch Grow", "Glitch Executor Labs", {legalEntity.name}, the cobra
        mascot, and related marks are property of {legalEntity.name}.
