        applicable law, (b) content you run on platforms through the
        Service, or (c) your breach of any connected platform's terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Governing law &amp; dispute resolution</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the
        <strong>{legalEntity.jurisdiction}</strong> and the federal laws of
        Canada applicable therein. Any dispute shall be finally resolved by
        <strong>binding arbitration</strong> administered by
        <strong>{legalEntity.arbitrationRules}</strong>, seated in
        <strong>{legalEntity.arbitrationSeat}</strong>, by a single
        arbitrator, in English. Each party waives jury trial and, to the
        maximum extent permitted, any right to participate in a class or
        representative proceeding. Nothing overrides non-waivable consumer
        rights under Ontario's Consumer Protection Act, 2002 or equivalent
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms. Material changes take effect no sooner
        than 30 days after the revised version is posted on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>13. General</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Severability, entire agreement, no waiver, assignment:</strong>
        unenforceable provisions are severed, these Terms and our Privacy
        Policy form the entire agreement, our failure to enforce is not a
        waiver, and you may not assign your rights (we may, on sale of
        assets or change of business form).
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${legalEntity.email}`}>{legalEntity.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-fluid-sm">
        {legalEntity.name}<br/>
        Attention: {legalEntity.owner}<br/>
